I sit by the window on the bus.
The morning sun is lovely and warm today.
It is summer in Copenhagen, and the city looks beautiful.
I look out at the familiar streets.
We drive past a large park with green trees.
People are already cycling on the bike paths.
I take this bus to my work every morning.
The route is exactly the same as in January.
But everything is completely different now.
I remember my first week here in the city.
It was freezing cold and very dark.
I did not know the neighborhood at all back then.
I was also very nervous about my new job at the software company.
Now I know exactly where we are.
I recognize the local baker and the square.
The bus stops, and more people get on.
I smile and lean back in my seat.
I am ready for a good day at the office.
